{
  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "Realty Income’s core model is owning and actively managing freestanding commercial properties under long-term net leases; tenants typically cover most property-level taxes, insurance, and maintenance. The 2025 10-K reported more than 15,500 properties across the U.S., U.K., and eight other European countries. This scale and geographic spread support recurring rent collection, while the supplied evidence does not quantify recession performance or tenant concentration.",
      "sourceIds": ["extended-sec-edgar-o-10k"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Operating momentum is positive but mixed in quality: revenue for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 rose 10.7% year over year, while operating cash flow rose 5.5%. The 10-Q attributes rental growth to acquisitions and reports same-store rental revenue growth of $37.9 million for the nine-month period. Because 2026 interim net income is not available on a comparable basis in the supplied SEC metrics, annual net-income growth should not be read as same-period evidence for this quarter.",
      "sourceIds": ["extended-sec-edgar-o-fundamentals", "extended-sec-edgar-o-10q"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Q3 AFFO per share increased 3.7% to $1.12, and management raised 2026 AFFO-per-share guidance to $4.45–$4.46 while reaffirming a $10 billion investment-volume target. The release also reported $2.6 billion invested at a 6.8% initial weighted-average cash yield and a 103.5% rent recapture rate on re-leased properties. These figures support the thesis that acquisitions and lease economics can sustain growth, though guidance and investment targets remain management statements.",
      "sourceIds": ["extended-sec-edgar-o-8k-0000726728-26-000056"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dividend durability is a central part of the income thesis, but growth appears modest. The 2025 10-K says the company had raised its dividend for more than 31 consecutive years; filed dividends per share grew at 2.7% CAGR over the three years through FY2025. The latest quote source reports a 5.52% indicated yield. News summaries cite AFFO coverage above 130% and a 73% payout ratio, but those figures are secondary-source claims and should be reconciled to the underlying filing before relying on them.",
      "sourceIds": ["extended-sec-edgar-o-10k", "extended-sec-edgar-o-fundamentals", "market-yahoo-equity-o", "news-equity-1", "news-equity-15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Funding costs and capital access are key thesis sensitivities. The 10-year Treasury yield was 4.88% on November 9, 2026, up from 4.86% on November 6; the 2-year yield was 4.56%, up from 4.51%. The Q3 release said the company had fully prefunded its equity needs for the remainder of 2026 and achieved an approximately 170-basis-point leverage-neutral investment spread. The supplied debt evidence is incomplete, so leverage and debt-service capacity cannot be independently assessed here.",
      "sourceIds": ["extended-fred-macro", "extended-sec-edgar-o-8k-0000726728-26-000056", "extended-sec-edgar-o-fundamentals"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Valuation evidence is mixed and incomplete. The quote snapshot reports 40.80x trailing P/E and 38.36x forward P/E, while market capitalization was about $56.8 billion and market cap to annualized revenue was 9.15x. Peer valuation supportability is marked not supportable, and EV-based measures are withheld because current SEC debt is incomplete. These limitations prevent a robust peer-relative or enterprise-value conclusion.",
      "sourceIds": ["market-yahoo-equity-o", "extended-sec-edgar-o-fundamentals"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Longer-term price performance has lagged the broad market in the supplied history: O returned 4.2% over one year, 19.0% over three years, and -15.1% over five years, versus SPY’s 11.2%, 72.4%, and 63.8% over the corresponding windows. These are price returns, not total returns, and therefore exclude dividends—an important limitation for an income-oriented REIT comparison.",
      "sourceIds": ["price-history-O", "price-history-SPY"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Recent technical evidence is constructive over the shorter term but mixed over the longer trend: the November 11 close of $59.57 was above the 50-day average of $56.98 and below the 200-day average of $61.55. The market snapshot shows a 0.05% 24-hour move on volume below its reported average. Technical indicators describe recent price behavior and do not establish operating fundamentals.",
      "sourceIds": ["verified-snapshot-O", "market-yahoo-equity-o"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Potential catalysts include execution of the $10 billion investment target, maintaining spreads between acquisition yields and financing costs, continued same-store rent growth, and development of the European private-capital platform. The Q3 release reported a strategic European joint venture with KKR supported by an initial €528 million investment; the supplied evidence does not quantify the venture’s expected earnings contribution or timing.",
      "sourceIds": ["extended-sec-edgar-o-8k-0000726728-26-000056"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The bear case centers on the combination of modest per-share growth, interest-rate sensitivity, acquisition competition, and potentially expensive equity valuation. A news summary reports an implied slowdown in AFFO growth from 6.6% in Q1 to 1.4% in Q4, but this is a secondary-source interpretation and the supplied primary excerpts do not verify that quarterly trajectory. The 10-K explicitly identifies competition for investment properties as a risk.",
      "sourceIds": ["news-equity-5", "extended-sec-edgar-o-10k"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The 2026 Promote Award Plan creates incentive awards tied to incentive allocations from designated funds and joint ventures, with bonus pools capped at 40% of such allocations. This may support investment-management growth and employee retention, but the filing excerpt does not quantify potential expense, participant allocations, or expected proceeds.",
      "sourceIds": ["extended-sec-edgar-o-8k-0000726728-26-000063"]
    }
  ],
  "dataGaps": [
    "Current debt is incomplete at September 30, 2026 because LoansPayable, NotesPayable, and SecuredDebt concepts are not incorporated into the debt measure; net debt, debt-to-market-cap, and EV-based valuation are therefore unavailable. Sources: extended-sec-edgar-o-fundamentals.",
    "Gross profit, operating income, capital expenditure, current assets, and current liabilities are missing from the supplied SEC company-facts evidence. This prevents calculation of margins, free-cash-flow measures, current ratio, and several coverage ratios. Sources: extended-sec-edgar-o-fundamentals; extended-sec-edgar-o-10q.",
    "The nine-month 2026 operating-cash-flow figure lacks a same-period net-income value in the supplied evidence, so cash conversion cannot be computed on a matched-period basis. Sources: extended-sec-edgar-o-fundamentals.",
    "Dividend coverage claims in news summaries are not accompanied by the underlying AFFO and dividend figures on a consistent period basis in the supplied primary excerpts. Verify numerator, denominator, period, and scope before treating coverage as established. Sources: news-equity-1; news-equity-15; extended-sec-edgar-o-8k-0000726728-26-000056.",
    "The supplied evidence does not provide geographic revenue shares, reportable-segment results, typical lease duration, tenant renewal rates, quantified rent increases at renewal, or measured recession performance. Sources: extended-sec-edgar-o-10k; extended-sec-edgar-o-10q.",
    "Analyst-estimate coverage and an authoritative analyst target range are unavailable; options data are also unavailable. Sources: sourceGaps; evidenceLanes.",
